mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>x</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>y</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>z</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>x</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>y</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> Prove that every model of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\tau\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> has an infinite domain. Where does\nyour proof use that domains are non-empty?</p>","file":"ch7/counter-models.html"}